    "title": "Crawler revamp, Phase 0: stop the damage now",
    "why": "Urgent. The crawler's 5-minute runs often end before they finish, and the site read that silence as results: websites taken off listings as 'unreachable', identity jobs' tries spent, every place from a source wiped by a read that never happened, a failed guide draft wiping its 'kept down' mark and hashes, a person's guide edit overwritten by a draft, and the monthly landmark load deleting held rows. This adds small guards in the current code so nothing more is lost while the revamp runs (review B5-B9), plus a read-only snapshot of each store in the daily health report (handoffs/crawler-revamp.md Phase 0). No database changes, no worker change.",
